    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Job’s Reply to Eliphaz"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then Job answered:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If only my grief could be weighed",
          "and my devastation placed with it on the scales."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For then it would outweigh the sand of the seas!",
          "That is why my words are rash."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Surely the arrows of the Almighty have pierced me;",
          "my spirit drinks their poison.",
          "God’s terrors are arrayed against me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Does a wild donkey bray over fresh grass",
          "or an ox low over its fodder?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Is bland food eaten without salt?",
          "Is there flavor in an egg white?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I refuse to touch them;",
          "they are like contaminated food."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If only my request would be granted",
          "and God would provide what I hope for:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "that he would decide to crush me,",
          "to unleash his power and cut me off!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "It would still bring me comfort,",
          "and I would leap for joy in unrelenting pain",
          "that I have not denied the words of the Holy One."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "What strength do I have, that I should continue to hope?",
          "What is my future, that I should be patient?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Is my strength that of stone,",
          "or my flesh made of bronze?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Since I cannot help myself,",
          "the hope for success has been banished from me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A despairing man should receive loyalty from his friends, ,",
          "even if he abandons the fear of the Almighty."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My brothers are as treacherous as a wadi,",
          "as seasonal streams that overflow"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "and become darkened because of ice,",
          "and the snow melts into them."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The wadis evaporate in warm weather;",
          "they disappear from their channels in hot weather."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Caravans turn away from their routes,",
          "go up into the desert, and perish."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The caravans of Tema look for these streams.",
          "The traveling merchants of Sheba hope for them."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They are ashamed because they had been confident of finding water.",
          "When they arrive there, they are disappointed."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "So this is what you have now become to me.",
          "When you see something dreadful, you are afraid."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Have I ever said, “Give me something”",
          "or “Pay a bribe for me from your wealth”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "or “Deliver me from the enemy’s hand”",
          "or “Redeem me from the hand of the ruthless”?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Teach me, and I will be silent.",
          "Help me understand what I did wrong."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "How painful honest words can be!",
          "But what does your rebuke prove?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Do you think that you can disprove my words",
          "or that a despairing man’s words are mere wind?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "No doubt you would cast lots for a fatherless child",
          "and negotiate a price to sell your friend."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But now, please look at me;",
          "I will not lie to your face."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          29
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Reconsider; don’t be unjust.",
          "Reconsider; my righteousness is still the issue."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          30
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Is there injustice on my tongue",
          "or can my palate not taste disaster?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
